'''Super Envy''' is a [[mini-boss]] and one of the [[Seven Deadly Sins#Super Sins|Seven Super Deadly Sins]]. He is randomly encountered as an alternate version of {{e|Envy}}.

== Behavior ==
* Super Envy floats around the room diagonally, bouncing off of the walls.
* Splits into three medium heads upon death which split into 2-3 small heads each when destroyed. These small heads split one last time into 2 even smaller heads when destroyed.
** The last head killed drops a {{e|Troll Bomb}} or {{i|Shoop da Whoop!|na+}} / {{I|Forever alone|a+}}.
* The heads increase in speed as they split into smaller versions.

== Notes ==
* {{dlc|nr}} Super Envy can drop {{i|Shoop da Whoop!|na+}} / {{i|Forever alone|a+}} even if Isaac has already encountered/possessed it.

== Trivia ==
* Like Envy, Super Envy's expressions are a reference to "rage comic" memes, with the biggest and smallest heads showing a [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/trollface troll face] and [https://knowyourmeme.com/memes/poker-face poker face], respectively.
** This is reinforced by his drops {{I|Shoop da Whoop!|na+}} / {{I|Forever alone|a+}}, both references to memes from the same era.
* Envy and Super Envy have a lower chance of dropping their item than the other sins.
* The [[wikipedia:Seven Deadly Sins|Seven Deadly Sins]] that these mini-bosses are based upon are, in Christian teachings, a classification of vices from which all others are derived.
* {{dlc|a+}} Until patch [[v1.06.J149]], Super Envy had a chance to spawn a {{i|Shoop da Whoop!}} instead of a {{i|Forever alone}}. According to the developers, he was always intended to drop {{i|Forever alone}}, but the behavior has been bugged since the initial port of the game.
* {{dlc|r}} Super Envy is the only Super Sin whose [[Stage HP]] wasn't increased in Repentance.

